  "result": "Perfect! All 184 tests pass. I've successfully implemented customer statements:\n\n**Created `src/statements.js` with `statement(customerId, invoices, asOf)` function:**\n\n- Generates a customer statement listing unpaid invoices up to a given date\n- Returns `ok({ customerId, invoices, totalDue })`\n- Each invoice in statement includes:\n  - `number`: Invoice number\n  - `issueDate`: When the invoice was issued\n  - `dueDate`: When payment is due\n  - `total`: Full invoice total (from invoiceTotals)\n  - `due`: Amount still owed (from balanceDue)\n- `totalDue`: Sum of all due amounts\n- Filters to only include:\n  - Invoices for the specified customer (ID normalized)\n  - Status 'issued' or 'partially_paid' (excludes draft and paid)\n  - Issue dates on or before the asOf cutoff date\n- Sorted by issueDate (oldest first)\n- Returns CUSTOMER_NOT_FOUND for unknown customers\n- Returns DATE_INVALID for invalid asOf dates\n\n**Updated `issueInvoice()` to preserve:**\n- terms and dueDate (payment terms)\n- voucher (if applied)\n- payments (if any recorded)\n\n**Comprehensive tests covering:**\n- Empty statements\n- Single and multiple invoices per customer\n- Status filtering (draft excluded, paid excluded)\n- Date filtering (before, on, after asOf)\n- Multiple customers (proper filtering)\n- Correct due calculations (unpaid vs. partially paid)\n- Proper sorting by issueDate\n- Edge cases (exact date matches, boundary conditions)\n\n**Example statement:**\n```\nCustomer C-003 statement as of 2026-10-31:\n- INV-2026-0001: Issued 2026-10-07, Due 2026-10-21, Total \u20ac1,452.00, Due \u20ac1,452.00\n- INV-2026-0002: Issued 2026-10-15, Due 2026-11-04, Total \u20ac1,452.00, Due \u20ac952.00\nTotal Due: \u20ac2,404.00\n```",
